Host-side gtest unit tests for crosspoint-reader.

Build and run:

  cmake -S test -B build/test
  cmake --build build/test
  ctest --test-dir build/test --output-on-failure -j

Run a single suite directly:

  cmake --build build/test --target StreamingJsonParserTest
  build/test/streaming_json_parser/StreamingJsonParserTest --gtest_filter='*'

Google Test is fetched via CMake FetchContent on first configure; the pinned
version lives in test/CMakeLists.txt.

Two targets here are host tools, not gtest suites, so ctest does not run them:

  map_preview  renders a map frame with the device's own MapRenderer --
               docs/device-preview.md (parent repo)
  map_replay   replays a recorded ride through the device's own
               MapFollow::decide() and counts redraws, with a threshold sweep
               -- docs/map-follow.md, "Sweeping the thresholds off the device"

A new file under src/ that a *shared* unit calls -- MapRenderer,
MapPreviewPipeline, anything several suites link -- must be added to **every**
test target that links that unit, not only to the new suite's own
CMakeLists.txt. The symptom is a link error that reads like a missing
implementation:

  undefined reference to `MapPointSource::MapPointSource(IFileSource&, ...)'

MapTileReaderGoldenTest stopped linking when the point layer landed, because
test/map_tile_reader/CMakeLists.txt never gained MapPointReader.cpp,
MapPointSource.cpp and MapPointMarks.cpp while MapRenderer.cpp started calling
into them. Fixed 2026-08-22. Grep the new file's class name across
test/*/CMakeLists.txt after adding one.
